Z||000002||rx7speed||09-23-2001||05:29 AM||||if you dont have emissions why get a free flowing cat?<P>I tried gutting mine (have 3 on my RX-7) and noticed a difference but then later installed a header straight pipe and the difference from gutted cats was quit a bit.<P>the cats even though wihtout guts creat turbulent air. the quick opening and then closing slow down the air and make eddies and then fight itself.<P>just go out and get a straight pipe. and for you gus with emissions just keep your old cat and put it in during emission time.<P><BR>oh yeah how the heck did you get out of having a cat in your state orief<P>------------------<BR>who needs pistons I have rotary<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||09-23-2001||08:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rx7speed:<BR><B>oh yeah how the heck did you get out of having a cat in your state orief<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In our state if you insure/register your car as a classic/showcar they allow you to exempt the car from emission testing. Also it is insured for the appraised value.<BR>There are mileage restrictions (3400 per year) but since I store it in the winter and only drive it on the weekends, It's not a problem for me. Some insurance companies don't have mileage restrictions. You can check with your local EPA office and see if your state offers the same thing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||09-23-2001||02:32 PM||||I had the converter taken out. It was time for a replacement, but I didn't have the money for a new one. So now there's just a straight pipe there. It's a little louder, and illegal, but that's ok. We don't have emmisions testing here. At least I've never had to get mine tested. If you're worried about getting caught, put in a straight pipe, and cover it with the old converter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||09-23-2001||05:56 PM||||For anyone running without a cat, just be aware, it's a Federal offense to defeat the emissions controls in any way.  Even if you can legally get an exemtion (Lucky you, Orief!), it's still against Federal Law to tamper with it.  No, it's not likely the FBI is gonna really care, but be aware of it and make your own, informed choices.||||reg||4
Z||000006||artherd||09-23-2001||07:02 PM||||The GM catalysts were horriblely restrictive...<P>Rodney's stainless cat is far far better than OE, and is even better than a straight pipe.<P>ALl of you with 'no cat' are not only polluting the air I breathe, but you're *sacraficing* horsepower, and breaking several Federal laws (even if your state OKs it...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||09-23-2001||08:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B><BR>ALl of you with 'no cat' are not only polluting the air I breathe, but you're *sacraficing* horsepower, and breaking several Federal laws (even if your state OKs it...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's why I also smoke, so I can give you cancer with secondary smoke!<P>And if you think we are loosing power, it doesn't show on my flow bench or at the drag strip...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rx7speed||09-24-2001||04:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B><BR>ALl of you with 'no cat' are not only polluting the air I breathe, but you're *sacraficing* horsepower, and breaking several Federal laws (even if your state OKs it...)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yeah I agree my car stinks a little but as for loosing HP??? I had three fricken cats on my car<BR>took them out and put a header on there with straight pipe and cut about a second off my 0-60 <P>though I dont have a fiero... yet...<BR>putting my RX7 in the shop while I get a new motor put in and some suspension stuff. while I am doing this though I need another car... thinking fiero or MR2||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||09-24-2001||05:22 AM||||shrug, do unto others....<P>Not all cats are created equal, infact far from it.  I stand behind the statment that a new, stainless steel, high-flow catalyst is the best intermediary in a Fiero's exhaust system.<P>I would however not recomend three of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||falconhulk||09-24-2001||08:38 AM||||ahhhh this post is strange because I work in Virginia and I am pretty sure there are emmisions laws in Virginia.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||09-24-2001||09:56 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>For anyone running without a cat, just be aware, it's a Federal offense to defeat the emissions controls in any way.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Federal EPA also allows exemtions on special purpose cars. This includes but not limited to: Race cars, Showcars, cars prior to 1967, etc. These are allowed because the vehicles are either only used for a very limited time or used in an "off road" environment. The exclusions were added in the early 90's because of many special interest groups like SCCA, SEMA, NHRA, etc. Licensing of the vehicle is the decision of the local states which have certain restrictions as to what can be done to the vehicle. This varies by state. In my state the classification of "showcar" allows engine mods and swaps but you must maintain DOT approved street tires, all working lights, (head, tail, brakes, turn, etc) safety equipment, (Bumpers, seat belts, etc) and a quiet exhaust when driving on the street. The state also requires an endorsement or rider as to the purpose of the vehicle. I looked into the "legallity" of all of this before. <P>Originally posted by artherd:<BR>"ALl of you with 'no cat' are not only polluting the air I breathe, but you're *sacraficing* horsepower, and breaking several Federal laws (even if your state OKs it...)"<P><BR>Sorry but I actually gained horsepower. As for polluting the air you breathe, There is more pollution (In parts per million) in the air during rush hour traffic than what comes out of my car. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||NEPTUNE||09-24-2001||02:10 PM||||ALL pollution is bad- no matter how little.<BR>Flowmaster makes a free flow cat, BTW.  <BR>And if you are one of the 25% of the US population who still chooses to smoke cigarettes, PLEASE use your ashtray- you have two of them, and all litter is bad, too- no matter how little. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||6
